<title>POLAND: FORECAST-Polish 52-wk,13-wk T-bill yield seen down.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Polish 52-wk,13-wk T-bill yield seen down.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banks expect the average yield on Poland's benchmark 52-week T-bill to fall to 18.40 percent at the end of 1997 against 21.39 percent at Monday's primary sale, a Reuters poll of the country's 26 largest banks showed.</p>
<p>The average yield on the 13-week T-bill was also seen falling to 18.00 percent by year-end from 20.82 percent at today's primary auction, the poll showed.</p>
<p>		     MAY	   END-97	  12-MONTHS AHEAD</p>
<p> 52-WEEK AVG   21.34	18.40 (18.57)     17.42 (17.67)</p>
<p>     MINIMUM   20.63	16.50 (17.0)	15.80 (16.0)</p>
<p>     MAXIMUM   21.65	20.60 (20.6)	21.40 (19.5)</p>
<p> 13-WEEK AVG   20.90	18.00 (18.31)     17.05 (17.39)</p>
<p>     MINIMUM   20.15	15.90 (16.5)	14.50 (14.75)</p>
<p>     MAXIMUM   21.40	20.35 (19.9)	21.20 (19.0)</p>
<p>NOTE: In brackets previous figures for end-97 and April-98 from last month's poll.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
